  "Question": "Which of the following conditions establishes that parallelogram \\(ABCD\\) is a rhombus?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(AC=BD\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\angle A=90^\\circ\\)",
    "C": "\\(AB\\parallel CD\\)",
    "D": "\\(AB=BC\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A parallelogram with a pair of equal adjacent sides is a rhombus. Either \\(AC=BD\\) or \\(\\angle A=90^\\circ\\) establishes that it is a rectangle, while \\(AB\\parallel CD\\) is already a property of a parallelogram.",
